# nexus-core — nightly database backup (example crontab entries)
#
# Install with:
#   crontab -e        # then paste one of the lines below
#
# 1) Native cron on the host (needs postgresql-client for pg_dump):
#
# 15 2 * * * cd /srv/nexus-core && \
#   PGHOST=127.0.0.1 PGPORT=5432 PGUSER=nexus PGDBASE=nexus PGPASSWORD="$(grep -m1 '^DB_PASSWORD=' .env | cut -d= -f2-)" \
#   BACKUP_DIR=/srv/nexus-core/backups BACKUP_KEEP_DAYS=7 \
#   ./scripts/backup_db.sh >> /var/log/nexus-backup.log 2>&1
#
# 2) Docker compose (no pg_dump on the host needed):
#
# 15 2 * * * cd /srv/nexus-core && \
#   docker compose --profile backup run --rm backup >> /var/log/nexus-backup.log 2>&1
#
# 3) Termux (phone) — cron is unavailable; use this in a script run by
#    `termux-job-scheduler` or by hand:
#
#   docker compose --profile backup run --rm backup   # not available on the phone
#   ./scripts/backup_db.sh                            # needs pg_dump in PATH
#
# Notes:
# * The script exits 3 when another run still holds the lock — a slow dump never
#   gets joined by a second one.
# * Rotation only touches "${BACKUP_PREFIX}-db-*.sql.gz" inside BACKUP_DIR; it
#   never deletes anything else.
# * Restore:   gunzip -c backups/nexus-db-YYYYmmdd-HHMMSS.sql.gz | psql -h HOST -U USER -d DB
